IMPORT prelude

-- Residential Property Act 1976 (Singapore) -- who is a foreign person (s 2), what is residential and what is non-restricted
-- residential property (ss 2, 4), the prohibition on foreign acquisition and its voidness (s 3(1), (2)), the 7-year lease and
-- mortgage carve-outs (ss 3(1)(c), 4(7), 33(b), (d)), inheritance by a foreign heir (s 3(3), (4), (13)), the duty of former
-- citizens and permanent residents to sell (s 3A), the whole-development offence (s 4(2), (3)), foreign mortgagees (s 22),
-- nominee purchases (s 23), approval of natural persons (s 25(5)), the financial penalty and offence for breaching approval
-- conditions (ss 25B, 25C), foreign governments and religious groups (s 30), and the general penalty, officers' liability and
-- composition (ss 36, 36A).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RPA1976.txt. The revised
-- edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; later annotations seen in the body are S 26/2022
-- (wef 13 January 2022, s 4(4)) and Act 25 of 2021 (wef 1 April 2022, s 24(8)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a buyer, seller, heir,
-- mortgagee or conveyancer meets. Not encoded: foreign companies holding since 1973 and the Controller's attach-and-sell machinery
-- (ss 5-8, 6A), conversion and vesting of Singapore entities (ss 9-18, 26, 27), transfer particulars and Registrar powers
-- (ss 19, 20, 24), confiscation orders (ss 4A, 23A), sale directions and change of use (ss 28, 28A), housing developers (s 31),
-- appeals (s 31A), the Minister's exemptions (s 32) beyond the s 32(2C) penalty, rulings (s 34), and the Schedules of HUDC flats.
-- The Minister's discretions are inputs, not rules.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Residential Property Act 1976 -- foreign acquisition`

§§ `2 -- who is a foreign person`

-- s 2: "foreign person" means any person who is not (a) a citizen of Singapore; (b) a Singapore company; (c) a Singapore limited
-- liability partnership; (d) a Singapore society. A permanent resident is not on that list.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `a Singapore citizen`
    `a Singapore company`
    `a Singapore LLP`
    `a Singapore society`
    `a permanent resident`
    `a foreign individual`
    `a foreign company`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a foreign person` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a Singapore citizen` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Singapore company` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Singapore LLP` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Singapore society` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 2: "Singapore company" -- (a) "incorporated in Singapore and its directors and members are all citizens"; (b) a corporate
-- member must itself satisfy (a); (c) and so on up the chain. "Member" includes the beneficiary of a share held in trust.
-- Simplified here to three facts; the chain test is folded into "every member is a citizen or a Singapore company".
GIVEN `incorporated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `every director is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `every member is a citizen or a Singapore company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company is a Singapore company` IF
    `incorporated in Singapore` AND `every director is a citizen` AND `every member is a citizen or a Singapore company`

§§ `2, 4 -- residential and non-restricted residential property`

-- s 2: "residential property" includes vacant land, dwelling houses, land zoned residential, but "does not include" land or
-- premises permitted to be used "solely for industrial or commercial purposes" or "any hotel registered under ... the Hotels Act".
-- s 4(1): the Act "does not apply" to a foreign person's acquisition of (a) a flat in a residential development "that is not a
-- landed dwelling house"; (b) "any unit comprised in a development ... bearing the title 'condominium'"; (c) an executive
-- condominium unit. s 4(10): "landed dwelling house" means a detached, semi-detached or terrace house "whether or not comprised
-- within a strata title plan"; "unit" includes a flat or dwelling house. s 2: "non-restricted residential property" means property
-- described in s 4(1) but not in s 4(2).
DECLARE Property IS ONE OF
    `a landed house`
    `a flat in a residential building`
    `a condominium unit`
    `a strata landed house in a condominium development`
    `an executive condominium unit`
    `vacant land zoned residential`
    `a registered hotel`
    `premises used solely for commercial purposes`

GIVEN `the property` IS A Property
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property is residential property` IF
    CONSIDER `the property`
    WHEN `a registered hotel` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `premises used solely for commercial purposes` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- A strata landed house inside a development titled "condominium" is read here as within s 4(1)(b), because (b) says "any unit"
-- and "unit" includes a dwelling house. That is a reading of the words, not a ruling; s 34 lets the Minister rule conclusively.
GIVEN `the property` IS A Property
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property is within section 4(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the property`
    WHEN `a flat in a residential building` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a condominium unit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a strata landed house in a condominium development` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an executive condominium unit` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3, 4, 25, 33 -- the prohibition and its exceptions`

-- s 3(1)(c): "a foreign person must not purchase or acquire any residential property ... except by way of a mortgage, charge or
-- reconveyance"; s 3(2): any such purchase or acquisition "is void". s 33(b): nothing prohibits a mortgage to a foreign person.
-- s 33(d): nothing prevents a foreign person "from acquiring any estate or interest under any agreement, lease or deed of
-- assignment" provided no term exceeds "7 years at any one time, inclusive of any further term ... by way of an option for renewal".
-- s 4(2): even for non-restricted property, a foreign person must not "without the prior approval of the Minister" acquire "all
-- the flats" or "all the units" in a development; s 4(7): leases up to 7 years are again excepted. s 25(2): a foreign person who
-- wants restricted property "must apply to the Minister"; once approved under s 25 the person is an "approved purchaser" (s 2).
GIVEN `lease term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interest is a short lease` IF
    `lease term in years` GREATER THAN 0 AND `lease term in years` AT MOST 7

GIVEN `the buyer` IS A Person, `the property` IS A Property, `by way of mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN, `lease term in years` IS A NUMBER,
      `all the units in the development` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Minister's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the acquisition is prohibited` IF
        `the person is a foreign person` `the buyer`
    AND `the property is residential property` `the property`
    AND (NOT `by way of mortgage`)
    AND (NOT `the interest is a short lease` `lease term in years`)
    AND (NOT `has the Minister's approval`)
    AND (    (NOT `the property is within section 4(1)` `the property`)
          OR `all the units in the development`)

-- s 4(3): contravening s 4(2) is an offence, "a fine not exceeding $100,000" (no imprisonment is provided).
GIVEN `the buyer` IS A Person, `the property` IS A Property, `lease term in years` IS A NUMBER,
      `all the units in the development` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Minister's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the whole-development offence is committed` IF
        `the person is a foreign person` `the buyer`
    AND `the property is within section 4(1)` `the property`
    AND `all the units in the development`
    AND (NOT `has the Minister's approval`)
    AND (NOT `the interest is a short lease` `lease term in years`)

`the maximum fine for the whole-development offence` MEANS 100000

§§ `3(3), (4), (13) -- a foreign heir`

-- s 3(3): "No estate or interest in any residential property belonging to a deceased person who dies on or after 11 September
-- 1973 passes by bequest, succession or inheritance to any foreign person". s 3(4): the personal representatives "are ... bound to
-- sell" to a citizen or approved purchaser "within a period of 5 years from the date of the death", or any extension under
-- s 3(12), and pay the net proceeds to the foreign heir. s 3(13): "The provisions of this Act do not apply to a foreign person who is
-- a surviving joint tenant". s 3(3) is not itself limited to restricted property; this encoding lets s 4(1) carve out non-restricted
-- property (INFERENCE: s 4(1) speaks of "transfer ... purchase or acquisition", and inheritance is read as an acquisition).
GIVEN `the heir` IS A Person, `the property` IS A Property, `surviving joint tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interest passes to the heir` IF
        (NOT `the person is a foreign person` `the heir`)
    OR  (NOT `the property is residential property` `the property`)
    OR  `the property is within section 4(1)` `the property`
    OR  `surviving joint tenant`

GIVEN `years since the death` IS A NUMBER, `extension allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the personal representatives are out of time to sell` IF
    `years since the death` GREATER THAN 5 AND (NOT `extension allowed`)

§§ `3A -- former citizens and permanent residents`

-- s 3A(1): an individual who acquired restricted residential property "as a citizen or permanent resident" and then (a) renounces
-- or is deprived of citizenship on or after 17 January 2011, or (b) cancels PR on or after that date "other than on the ground of
-- becoming a citizen of Singapore", or has PR terminated, "must sell ... within a period of 2 years from the date of cessation",
-- or any longer period the Minister allows "before the end of those 2 years". (2): "$20,000 or ... 3 years or ... both".
GIVEN `acquired as citizen or PR` IS A BOOLEAN, `the property` IS A Property, `date status ceased` IS A NUMBER,
      `ceased PR on becoming a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the former citizen or PR must sell` IF
        `acquired as citizen or PR`
    AND `the property is residential property` `the property`
    AND (NOT `the property is within section 4(1)` `the property`)
    AND `date status ceased` AT LEAST 20110117
    AND (NOT `ceased PR on becoming a citizen`)

GIVEN `acquired as citizen or PR` IS A BOOLEAN, `the property` IS A Property, `date status ceased` IS A NUMBER,
      `ceased PR on becoming a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `years since cessation` IS A NUMBER, `longer period allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 3A offence is committed` IF
        `the former citizen or PR must sell` `acquired as citizen or PR` `the property` `date status ceased` `ceased PR on becoming a citizen`
    AND `years since cessation` GREATER THAN 2
    AND (NOT `longer period allowed`)

`the maximum fine under section 3A` MEANS 20000

§§ `22 -- mortgagees`

-- s 22(1): a mortgagee exercising its power of sale over restricted property "must not transfer the estate or interest to a
-- foreign person". (2): a mortgagee who forecloses or becomes vested "must sell to a citizen or an approved purchaser ... within a
-- period of 3 years"; (4): subsections (2) to (3) "apply only to mortgagees who are foreign persons".
GIVEN `the mortgagee` IS A Person, `the property` IS A Property
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the foreclosing mortgagee must sell within 3 years` IF
        `the person is a foreign person` `the mortgagee`
    AND `the property is residential property` `the property`
    AND (NOT `the property is within section 4(1)` `the property`)

§§ `23 -- nominees`

-- s 23(1): (a) a citizen or approved purchaser "must not purchase or acquire" restricted property "as a nominee of any foreign
-- person with the intention that [it] is to hold it in trust for that foreign person"; (b) the foreign person must not appoint such
-- a nominee. (2): the trust "is void and there is no resulting trust in favour of the foreign person". (4): "$100,000 or ...
-- 3 years or ... both".
GIVEN `the property` IS A Property, `bought as nominee for a foreign person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intended to hold in trust for that foreign person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the nominee offence is committed` IF
        `the property is residential property` `the property`
    AND (NOT `the property is within section 4(1)` `the property`)
    AND `bought as nominee for a foreign person`
    AND `intended to hold in trust for that foreign person`

`the maximum fine for the nominee offence` MEANS 100000

§§ `25(5) -- approval for a natural person's own home`

-- s 25(5): the Minister may approve an applicant, "being a natural person", who intends to buy "for the purpose of the
-- applicant's own occupation and that of the applicant's family as a dwelling house and not for the purpose of rental", where the
-- applicant (a) "is a permanent resident"; (b) is in the Minister's opinion of economic benefit or able to make an adequate
-- economic contribution; or (c) has qualifications or experience of value to Singapore. Approval remains discretionary (s 25(10)).
GIVEN `for own and family occupation only` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `of economic benefit in the Minister's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN, `has qualifications of value in the Minister's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant is within section 25(5)` IF
        `for own and family occupation only`
    AND (    `is a permanent resident`
          OR `of economic benefit in the Minister's opinion`
          OR `has qualifications of value in the Minister's opinion`)

§§ `25B, 25C -- breaching approval conditions`

-- s 25B(1): where an approved purchaser lets restricted property in contravention of an occupation condition (s 25(7)(a)), the
-- Controller may require a financial penalty "not exceeding the highest of" (a) $10,000; (b) "3 times the amount of rental payable
-- and collected" during the contravention; (c) "3 times the assessed rental reasonably expected to be collected". (For leases made
-- before 17 January 2011 only the period on or after that date counts; not encoded.)
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF `a` GREATER THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `rent collected` IS A NUMBER, `assessed rental` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum section 25B penalty` MEANS
    `the larger of` 10000 (`the larger of` (3 TIMES `rent collected`) (3 TIMES `assessed rental`))

-- s 25C: failing any other approval condition is an offence, "a fine not exceeding $200,000 or ... 3 years or ... both" and "a
-- further fine not exceeding $2,000 for every day" a continuing offence continues after conviction.
GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum section 25C fine` MEANS 200000 PLUS 2000 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

§§ `30 -- foreign governments and religious groups`

-- s 30(1): a foreign government, its accredited agent, or "any religious group in Singapore" buying restricted property for
-- official purposes or its use "is not bound by the procedures laid down in section 25 but must first seek the written permission
-- of the Minister". (3): no permission needed for "a leasehold estate or interest for a term not exceeding 7 years".
GIVEN `the property` IS A Property, `lease term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister's written permission is needed under section 30` IF
        `the property is residential property` `the property`
    AND (NOT `the property is within section 4(1)` `the property`)
    AND (NOT `the interest is a short lease` `lease term in years`)

§§ `36, 36A -- general penalty, officers, composition`

-- s 36(1): contravention with no express penalty -- "$20,000 or ... 3 years or ... both". (3): where a company or other body
-- offends, every director, partner, manager, secretary or other officer "shall be deemed to be guilty". (4): defence if the
-- individual "proves that the offence was committed without his or her consent or connivance AND that he or she exercised such
-- diligence" as ought to have been exercised.
`the general maximum fine` MEANS 20000

GIVEN `the body offended` IS A BOOLEAN, `was an officer at the time` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is guilty` IF
        `the body offended`
    AND `was an officer at the time`
    AND (NOT (`proved no consent or connivance` AND `proved due diligence`))

-- s 36A(1): the Controller may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding
-- $10,000"; (3) no further proceedings after payment.
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition is within power` IF
    `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` AND `sum` AT MOST 10000
